  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-24T16:33:15.338Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Problem\nIf an Animator and an UdonBehaviour are components of the same GameObject, the Root Motion setting in the animator is disabled.\n# Why it's a problem\nRoot Motion is normally **enabled** by default on Animators. Adding an UdonBehaviour can unexpectedly break animators.\n# Workarounds\n- Don't put Animators and UdonBehaviours onto the same object if you want to use root motion. (However, this prevents us from using Animation Events!)\n- Use the following U# code proposed by CyanLaser\n```\nOnAnimatorMove() {\n     animator.ApplyDefaultRootMotion();\n}\n```\n# Proposed fix\nAdd a toggle to UdonBehaviours which lets us directly control the root motion setting.\n# Related\nhttps://ask.vrchat.com/t/fix-for-animator-apply-root-motion-position-and-rotation/296",
